{"id":"mahabharata-6-114","work":"mahabharata","part":6,"partName":"भीष्मपर्व","partNameEn":"Bhishma Parva","unit":114,"title":"चतुर्दशाधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 114 · The fall of Bhishma","summary":{"en":"The Pandavas, with Shikhandin in front, surround Bhishma and pierce him with countless weapons, and Arjuna's arrows strike him at every limb. At sunset Bhishma falls from his chariot onto a bed of arrows, with his body held up by the shafts and his head hanging.","kn":"ಶಿಖಂಡಿಯನ್ನು ಮುಂದಿಟ್ಟು ಪಾಂಡವರು ಭೀಷ್ಮನನ್ನು ಸುತ್ತುವರಿದು ಅಸಂಖ್ಯ ಆಯುಧಗಳಿಂದ ಚುಚ್ಚುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಅರ್ಜುನನ ಬಾಣಗಳು ಅವನ ಪ್ರತಿ ಅಂಗವನ್ನೂ ಭೇದಿಸುತ್ತವೆ. ಸೂರ್ಯಾಸ್ತದಲ್ಲಿ ಭೀಷ್ಮ ರಥದಿಂದ ಬಾಣಶಯ್ಯೆಯ ಮೇಲೆ ಬೀಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅವನ ದೇಹ ಬಾಣಗಳ ಮೇಲೆ ನೆಲ ಮುಟ್ಟದೆ ನಿಲ್ಲುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"शिखण्डी को आगे रखकर पाण्डव भीष्म को घेरते हैं और असंख्य शस्त्रों से बींधते हैं, अर्जुन के बाण उनके हर अंग को भेदते हैं। सूर्यास्त पर भीष्म रथ से बाणशय्या पर गिरते हैं और उनका शरीर बाणों पर टिका रहता है।","te":"శిఖండిని ముందుంచి పాండవులు భీష్ముని చుట్టుముట్టి లెక్కలేని ఆయుధాలతో గుచ్చుతారు; అర్జునుని బాణాలు ప్రతి అంగాన్ని ఛేదిస్తాయి. సూర్యాస్తమయంలో భీష్ముడు రథం నుండి బాణశయ్యపై పడతాడు; శరీరం నేలను తాకకుండా బాణాలపై నిలుస్తుంది.","ta":"சிகண்டியை முன்வைத்துப் பாண்டவர் பீஷ்மரைச் சூழ்ந்து எண்ணற்ற ஆயுதங்களால் துளைக்க, அர்ஜுனனின் அம்புகள் அவர் உறுப்புகளையெல்லாம் பிளக்கின்றன. சூரிய அஸ்தமனத்தில் பீஷ்மர் தேரிலிருந்து அம்புப் படுக்கையில் வீழ்கிறார்; உடல் அம்புகள் மேல் தரை தொடாமல் நிற்கிறது.","ml":"ശിഖണ്ഡിയെ മുന്നിൽ നിർത്തി പാണ്ഡവർ ഭീഷ്മരെ വളയുന്നു; എണ്ണമറ്റ ആയുധങ്ങൾകൊണ്ട് അദ്ദേഹത്തെ തുളയ്ക്കുന്നു, അർജുനന്റെ അമ്പുകൾ അദ്ദേഹത്തിന്റെ ഓരോ അവയവത്തിലും പതിക്കുന്നു. സൂര്യാസ്തമയത്തിൽ ഭീഷ്മർ അമ്പുകളുടെ ശയ്യയിൽ രഥത്തിൽനിന്ന് വീഴുന്നു; അമ്പുകൾ അദ്ദേഹത്തിന്റെ ശരീരത്തെ താങ്ങിനിർത്തുന്നു, തല താഴോട്ട് തൂങ്ങുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 6.114; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 26 2021","sections":[{"title":"भीष्मवधपर्व","titleEn":"Bhishmavadha Parva (The fall of Bhishma)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"एवं ते पाण्डवाः सर्वे पुरस्कृत्य शिखण्डिनम् ।\nविव्यधुः समरे भीष्मं परिवार्य समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So all the Pandavas, putting Shikhandi in front, surrounded Bhishma on every side and pierced him in the battle."}},{"n":2,"text":"शतघ्नीभिः सुघोराभिः पट्टिशैः सपरश्वधैः ।\nमुद्गरैर्मुसलैः प्रासैः क्षेपणीभिश्च सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With terrible hundred-slayers, with battle-axes and spears, with clubs, pestles and lances and with slings from every side,"}},{"n":3,"text":"शरैः कनकपुङ्खैश्च शक्तितोमरकम्पनैः ।\nनाराचैर्वत्सदन्तैश्च भुशुण्डीभिश्च भारत ।\nअताडयन्रणे भीष्मं सहिताः सर्वसृञ्जयाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"with gold-feathered arrows, spears and javelins that shook as they flew, with iron arrows, calf-tooth darts and fire-lances, O Bharata, all the Srinjayas together struck Bhishma in the battle."}},{"n":4,"text":"स विशीर्णतनुत्राणः पीडितो बहुभिस्तदा ।\nविव्यथे नैव गाङ्गेयो भिद्यमानेषु मर्मसु ॥","meaning":{"en":"His armor shattered and hurt by many, the son of Ganga did not flinch even as his vital parts were pierced."}},{"n":5,"text":"स दीप्तशरचापार्चिरस्त्रप्रसृतमारुतः ।\nनेमिनिर्ह्रादसंनादो महास्त्रोदयपावकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With blazing arrows and bow as flames, the winds of his weapons as drafts, the rumble of his chariot wheels as roaring, and his great weapons as the rising fire,"}},{"n":6,"text":"चित्रचापमहाज्वालो वीरक्षयमहेन्धनः ।\nयुगान्ताग्निसमो भीष्मः परेषां समपद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"with his bow a great and many-colored blaze and the death of heroes as his huge fuel, Bhishma became to his enemies like the fire at the end of an age."}},{"n":7,"text":"निपत्य रथसंघानामन्तरेण विनिःसृतः ।\nदृश्यते स्म नरेन्द्राणां पुनर्मध्यगतश्चरन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Falling upon the masses of chariots and breaking through them, he was seen moving again among the kings in the middle."}},{"n":8,"text":"ततः पाञ्चालराजं च धृष्टकेतुमतीत्य च ।\nपाण्डवानीकिनीमध्यमाससाद स वेगितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, passing the king of Panchala and Dhrishtaketu, he swiftly reached the middle of the Pandava army."}},{"n":9,"text":"ततः सात्यकिभीमौ च पाण्डवं च धनंजयम् ।\nद्रुपदं च विराटं च धृष्टद्युम्नं च पार्षतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he struck Satyaki, Bhima, the Pandava Arjuna, Drupada, Virata and Dhrishtadyumna son of Prishata,"}},{"n":10,"text":"भीमघोषैर्महावेगैर्वैरिवारणभेदिभिः ।\nषडेतान्षड्भिरानर्छद्भास्करप्रतिमैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"those six, with six very swift arrows, terrible in sound, that split the elephants of the enemy and shone like the sun."}},{"n":11,"text":"तस्य ते निशितान्बाणान्संनिवार्य महारथाः ।\nदशभिर्दशभिर्भीष्ममर्दयामासुरोजसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those great warriors turned away his sharp arrows and with great force wounded Bhishma with ten arrows each."}},{"n":12,"text":"शिखण्डी तु रणे बाणान्यान्मुमोच महाव्रते ।\nते भीष्मं विविशुस्तूर्णं स्वर्णपुङ्खाः शिलाशिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But the arrows that Shikhandi loosed at Bhishma of the great vow, gold-feathered and whetted on stone, quickly entered him."}},{"n":13,"text":"ततः किरीटी संरब्धो भीष्ममेवाभ्यवर्तत ।\nशिखण्डिनं पुरस्कृत्य धनुश्चास्य समाच्छिनत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the wearer of the diadem, Arjuna, enraged, came at Bhishma with Shikhandi in front and cut his bow."}},{"n":14,"text":"भीष्मस्य धनुषश्छेदं नामृष्यन्त महारथाः ।\nद्रोणश्च कृतवर्मा च सैन्धवश्च जयद्रथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"These great warriors could not bear the cutting of Bhishma's bow: Drona, Kritavarma, Jayadratha the Sindhu king,"}},{"n":15,"text":"भूरिश्रवाः शलः शल्यो भगदत्तस्तथैव च ।\nसप्तैते परमक्रुद्धाः किरीटिनमभिद्रुताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhurishravas, Shala, Shalya and Bhagadatta. Those seven, in a great rage, charged at the wearer of the diadem."}},{"n":16,"text":"उत्तमास्त्राणि दिव्यानि दर्शयन्तो महारथाः ।\nअभिपेतुर्भृशं क्रुद्धाश्छादयन्त स्म पाण्डवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Showing their supreme divine weapons, those great warriors, furiously angry, fell upon Arjuna and covered the Pandavas."}},{"n":17,"text":"तेषामापततां शब्दः शुश्रुवे फल्गुनं प्रति ।\nउद्वृत्तानां यथा शब्दः समुद्राणां युगक्षये ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sound of their charge at Phalguna was heard like the roar of the oceans breaking their bounds at the end of the age."}},{"n":18,"text":"हतानयत गृह्णीत युध्यतापि च कृन्तत ।\nइत्यासीत्तुमुलः शब्दः फल्गुनस्य रथं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Kill them! Bring them here! Seize them! Fight and cut them down!\" Such was the tumult of cries against Phalguna's chariot."}},{"n":19,"text":"तं शब्दं तुमुलं श्रुत्वा पाण्डवानां महारथाः ।\nअभ्यधावन्परीप्सन्तः फल्गुनं भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that uproar, the great warriors of the Pandavas, wishing to rescue Phalguna, rushed forward, O best of the Bharatas."}},{"n":20,"text":"सात्यकिर्भीमसेनश्च धृष्टद्युम्नश्च पार्षतः ।\nविराटद्रुपदौ चोभौ राक्षसश्च घटोत्कचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Satyaki, Bhimasena, Dhrishtadyumna son of Prishata, Virata and Drupada, the rakshasa Ghatotkacha,"}},{"n":21,"text":"अभिमन्युश्च संक्रुद्धः सप्तैते क्रोधमूर्छिताः ।\nसमभ्यधावंस्त्वरिताश्चित्रकार्मुकधारिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"and angry Abhimanyu, those seven, wild with rage and wielding marvelous bows, ran in haste."}},{"n":22,"text":"तेषां समभवद्युद्धं तुमुलं लोमहर्षणम् ।\nसंग्रामे भरतश्रेष्ठ देवानां दानवैरिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a tumultuous, hair-raising battle took place between them, best of the Bharatas, like that of gods against the Danavas."}},{"n":23,"text":"शिखण्डी तु रथश्रेष्ठो रक्ष्यमाणः किरीटिना ।\nअविध्यद्दशभिर्भीष्मं छिन्नधन्वानमाहवे ।\nसारथिं दशभिश्चास्य ध्वजं चैकेन चिच्छिदे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shikhandi, best of charioteers, protected by Arjuna, struck Bhishma, whose bow was cut, with ten arrows, and cut his charioteer with ten and his banner with one."}},{"n":24,"text":"सोऽन्यत्कार्मुकमादाय गाङ्गेयो वेगवत्तरम् ।\nतदप्यस्य शितैर्भल्लैस्त्रिभिश्चिच्छेद फल्गुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma took up another, faster bow, and Phalguna cut that too with three sharp broad arrows."}},{"n":25,"text":"एवं स पाण्डवः क्रुद्ध आत्तमात्तं पुनः पुनः ।\nधनुर्भीष्मस्य चिच्छेद सव्यसाची परंतपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus the angry Pandava Savyasachi, scourge of foes, again and again cut every bow Bhishma took up."}},{"n":26,"text":"स च्छिन्नधन्वा संक्रुद्धः सृक्किणी परिसंलिहन् ।\nशक्तिं जग्राह संक्रुद्धो गिरीणामपि दारणीम् ।\nतां च चिक्षेप संक्रुद्धः फल्गुनस्य रथं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"With his bow cut, Bhishma, furious, licked the corners of his mouth, and took up a spear that could split even mountains. Raging, he hurled it at Phalguna's chariot."}},{"n":27,"text":"तामापतन्तीं संप्रेक्ष्य ज्वलन्तीमशनीमिव ।\nसमादत्त शितान्भल्लान्पञ्च पाण्डवनन्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing it coming, blazing like a thunderbolt, the delight of the Pandavas took up five sharp broad arrows."}},{"n":28,"text":"तस्य चिच्छेद तां शक्तिं पञ्चधा पञ्चभिः शरैः ।\nसंक्रुद्धो भरतश्रेष्ठ भीष्मबाहुबलेरिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In his anger, best of the Bharatas, he cut that spear, which had been sent by Bhishma's arm strength, into five pieces with five arrows."}},{"n":29,"text":"सा पपात परिच्छिन्ना संक्रुद्धेन किरीटिना ।\nमेघवृन्दपरिभ्रष्टा विच्छिन्नेव शतह्रदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Cut by the enraged wearer of the diadem, it fell like lightning broken and dropped from a mass of clouds."}},{"n":30,"text":"छिन्नां तां शक्तिमालोक्य भीष्मः क्रोधसमन्वितः ।\nअचिन्तयद्रणे वीरो बुद्ध्या परपुरंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the spear cut, Bhishma, full of anger, that hero who conquers enemy cities, reflected in the battle."}},{"n":31,"text":"शक्तोऽहं धनुषैकेन निहन्तुं सर्वपाण्डवान् ।\nयद्येषां न भवेद्गोप्ता विष्वक्सेनो महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"With a single bow I could kill all the Pandavas, if the mighty Vishvaksena, Krishna, were not their protector."}},{"n":32,"text":"कारणद्वयमास्थाय नाहं योत्स्यामि पाण्डवैः ।\nअवध्यत्वाच्च पाण्डूनां स्त्रीभावाच्च शिखण्डिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For two reasons I will not fight the Pandavas: that the Pandavas must not be killed, and that Shikhandi was once a woman."}},{"n":33,"text":"पित्रा तुष्टेन मे पूर्वं यदा कालीमुदावहत् ।\nस्वच्छन्दमरणं दत्तमवध्यत्वं रणे तथा ।\nतस्मान्मृत्युमहं मन्ये प्राप्तकालमिवात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Long ago my father, pleased with me when he married Kali, granted me death at will and that I could not be killed in battle. So I think my own death has now come.\""}},{"n":34,"text":"एवं ज्ञात्वा व्यवसितं भीष्मस्यामिततेजसः ।\nऋषयो वसवश्चैव वियत्स्था भीष्ममब्रुवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Learning of the resolve of Bhishma of boundless power, the seers and the Vasus, standing in the sky, said to Bhishma,"}},{"n":35,"text":"यत्ते व्यवसितं वीर अस्माकं सुमहत्प्रियम् ।\nतत्कुरुष्व महेष्वास युद्धाद्बुद्धिं निवर्तय ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"What you have resolved, hero, is greatly dear to us. Do it, great archer: turn your mind from battle.\""}},{"n":36,"text":"तस्य वाक्यस्य निधने प्रादुरासीच्छिवोऽनिलः ।\nअनुलोमः सुगन्धी च पृषतैश्च समन्वितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When they had finished speaking, a fresh breeze blew, favorable and fragrant and mixed with drops of rain."}},{"n":37,"text":"देवदुन्दुभयश्चैव संप्रणेदुर्महास्वनाः ।\nपपात पुष्पवृष्टिश्च भीष्मस्योपरि पार्थिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Heavenly drums sounded with a great noise, and a shower of flowers fell on Bhishma, O king."}},{"n":38,"text":"न च तच्छुश्रुवे कश्चित्तेषां संवदतां नृप ।\nऋते भीष्मं महाबाहुं मां चापि मुनितेजसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"No one heard what they said to one another, king, except the mighty-armed Bhishma and me, through the power of the sage."}},{"n":39,"text":"संभ्रमश्च महानासीत्त्रिदशानां विशां पते ।\nपतिष्यति रथाद्भीष्मे सर्वलोकप्रिये तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great was the agitation of the gods, lord of the people, that Bhishma, dear to all the worlds, was about to fall from his chariot."}},{"n":40,"text":"इति देवगणानां च श्रुत्वा वाक्यं महामनाः ।\nततः शांतनवो भीष्मो बीभत्सुं नाभ्यवर्तत ।\nभिद्यमानः शितैर्बाणैः सर्वावरणभेदिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing the words of the host of gods, the great-minded son of Shantanu, Bhishma, did not turn against Bibhatsu, though he was pierced by sharp arrows that split all armor."}},{"n":41,"text":"शिखण्डी तु महाराज भरतानां पितामहम् ।\nआजघानोरसि क्रुद्धो नवभिर्निशितैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Shikhandi, great king, angrily struck the grandsire of the Bharatas in the chest with nine sharp arrows."}},{"n":42,"text":"स तेनाभिहतः संख्ये भीष्मः कुरुपितामहः ।\nनाकम्पत महाराज क्षितिकम्पे यथाचलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck by him in the battle, Bhishma, the grandsire of the Kurus, did not tremble, great king, like a mountain in an earthquake."}},{"n":43,"text":"ततः प्रहस्य बीभत्सुर्व्याक्षिपन्गाण्डिवं धनुः ।\nगाङ्गेयं पञ्चविंशत्या क्षुद्रकाणां समर्पयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bibhatsu, laughing, flexed his bow Gandiva and gave Bhishma twenty-five small arrows."}},{"n":44,"text":"पुनः शरशतेनैनं त्वरमाणो धनंजयः ।\nसर्वगात्रेषु संक्रुद्धः सर्वमर्मस्वताडयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Dhananjaya, quickly and in anger, struck him again with a hundred arrows in all his limbs and vital parts."}},{"n":45,"text":"एवमन्यैरपि भृशं वध्यमानो महारणे ।\nन चक्रुस्ते रुजं तस्य रुक्मपुङ्खाः शिलाशिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though struck so hard by others also in that great battle, their gold-feathered, stone-whetted arrows caused him no hurt."}},{"n":46,"text":"ततः किरीटी संरब्धो भीष्ममेवाभ्यवर्तत ।\nशिखण्डिनं पुरस्कृत्य धनुश्चास्य समाच्छिनत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the wearer of the diadem, in fury, came at Bhishma, with Shikhandi in front, and cut his bow."}},{"n":47,"text":"अथैनं दशभिर्विद्ध्वा ध्वजमेकेन चिच्छिदे ।\nसारथिं विशिखैश्चास्य दशभिः समकम्पयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he pierced him with ten arrows, cut his banner with one, and shook his charioteer with ten shafts."}},{"n":48,"text":"सोऽन्यत्कार्मुकमादत्त गाङ्गेयो बलवत्तरम् ।\nतदप्यस्य शितैर्भल्लैस्त्रिधा त्रिभिरुपानुदत् ।\nनिमेषान्तरमात्रेण आत्तमात्तं महारणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"The son of Ganga took up another, stronger bow, but Arjuna cut it too into three with three sharp arrows, in the space of a blink, each bow as he took it up in that great battle."}},{"n":49,"text":"एवमस्य धनूंष्याजौ चिच्छेद सुबहून्यपि ।\nततः शांतनवो भीष्मो बीभत्सुं नाभ्यवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"So he cut many bows of Bhishma in the fight. Then Bhishma, son of Shantanu, did not turn against Bibhatsu any more."}},{"n":50,"text":"अथैनं पञ्चविंशत्या क्षुद्रकाणां समर्दयत् ।\nसोऽतिविद्धो महेष्वासो दुःशासनमभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Arjuna pressed him hard with twenty-five small arrows. Badly wounded, the great archer spoke to Duhshasana."}},{"n":51,"text":"एष पार्थो रणे क्रुद्धः पाण्डवानां महारथः ।\nशरैरनेकसाहस्रैर्मामेवाभ्यसते रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"There is Arjuna, angry in the battle, the great warrior of the Pandavas, shooting me alone in the battle with many thousands of arrows."}},{"n":52,"text":"न चैष शक्यः समरे जेतुं वज्रभृता अपि ।\nन चापि सहिता वीरा देवदानवराक्षसाः ।\nमां चैव शक्ता निर्जेतुं किमु मर्त्याः सुदुर्बलाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even the wielder of the thunderbolt could not conquer him in the war, nor could gods, demons and rakshasas joined together; they could not defeat me either, so how could weak mortals?\""}},{"n":53,"text":"एवं तयोः संवदतोः फल्गुनो निशितैः शरैः ।\nशिखण्डिनं पुरस्कृत्य भीष्मं विव्याध संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"While they were speaking so, Phalguna, with Shikhandi in front, pierced Bhishma in the battle with sharp arrows."}},{"n":54,"text":"ततो दुःशासनं भूयः स्मयमानोऽभ्यभाषत ।\nअतिविद्धः शितैर्बाणैर्भृशं गाण्डीवधन्वना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, much wounded by the sharp arrows of the wielder of Gandiva, Bhishma smiled and spoke again to Duhshasana."}},{"n":55,"text":"वज्राशनिसमस्पर्शाः शिताग्राः संप्रवेशिताः ।\nविमुक्ता अव्यवच्छिन्ना नेमे बाणाः शिखण्डिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"These arrows, sharp-pointed, touching like thunderbolts, entering one after another without a break, are not Shikhandi's."}},{"n":56,"text":"निकृन्तमाना मर्माणि दृढावरणभेदिनः ।\nमुसलानीव मे घ्नन्ति नेमे बाणाः शिखण्डिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"These that cut my vital parts and split firm armor, striking me like pestles, are not Shikhandi's arrows."}},{"n":57,"text":"ब्रह्मदण्डसमस्पर्शा वज्रवेगा दुरासदाः ।\nमम प्राणानारुजन्ति नेमे बाणाः शिखण्डिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"These that touch like a brahmin's curse, strong as the thunderbolt and hard to withstand, and that tear at my life, are not Shikhandi's arrows."}},{"n":58,"text":"भुजगा इव संक्रुद्धा लेलिहाना विषोल्बणाः ।\nममाविशन्ति मर्माणि नेमे बाणाः शिखण्डिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"These that enter my vitals like angry snakes with licking tongues, full of venom, are not Shikhandi's arrows."}},{"n":59,"text":"नाशयन्तीव मे प्राणान्यमदूता इवाहिताः ।\nगदापरिघसंस्पर्शा नेमे बाणाः शिखण्डिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"These that kill me like hostile messengers of Yama, with the touch of maces and bars, are not Shikhandi's arrows."}},{"n":60,"text":"कृन्तन्ति मम गात्राणि माघमासे गवामिव ।\nअर्जुनस्य इमे बाणा नेमे बाणाः शिखण्डिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"These that cut my limbs like cold in the month of Magha cuts the cattle are Arjuna's arrows, not Shikhandi's."}},{"n":61,"text":"सर्वे ह्यपि न मे दुःखं कुर्युरन्ये नराधिपाः ।\nवीरं गण्डीवधन्वानमृते जिष्णुं कपिध्वजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"No other kings could cause me pain, all together, except the hero wielding Gandiva, the victorious ape-bannered Arjuna.\""}},{"n":62,"text":"इति ब्रुवञ्शांतनवो दिधक्षुरिव पाण्डवम् ।\nसविष्फुलिङ्गां दीप्ताग्रां शक्तिं चिक्षेप भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Saying this, as if wanting to burn the Pandava, the son of Shantanu hurled at him a spear, blazing at the tip and flying sparks, O Bharata."}},{"n":63,"text":"तामस्य विशिखैश्छित्त्वा त्रिधा त्रिभिरपातयत् ।\nपश्यतां कुरुवीराणां सर्वेषां तत्र भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Arjuna cut it with three broad arrows into three and dropped it, as all the Kuru heroes watched, Bharata."}},{"n":64,"text":"चर्माथादत्त गाङ्गेयो जातरूपपरिष्कृतम् ।\nखड्गं चान्यतरं प्रेप्सुर्मृत्योरग्रे जयाय वा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the son of Ganga took up a shield adorned with gold, and a sword, wanting either to die in front or to win."}},{"n":65,"text":"तस्य तच्छतधा चर्म व्यधमद्दंशितात्मनः ।\nरथादनवरूढस्य तदद्भुतमिवाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Arjuna's arrows shattered that shield into a hundred pieces, though Bhishma was armored and had not left his chariot, and it seemed a marvel."}},{"n":66,"text":"विनद्योच्चैः सिंह इव स्वान्यनीकान्यचोदयत् ।\nअभिद्रवत गाङ्गेयं मा वोऽस्तु भयमण्वपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Roaring loudly like a lion, Duryodhana urged his own divisions: \"Charge at the son of Ganga! Let there be no fear in you, not even a little!\""}},{"n":67,"text":"अथ ते तोमरैः प्रासैर्बाणौघैश्च समन्ततः ।\nपट्टिशैश्च सनिस्त्रिंशैर्नानाप्रहरणैस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then from every side they rushed at him alone with spears, lances and showers of arrows, with clubs and swords, and with many other weapons,"}},{"n":68,"text":"वत्सदन्तैश्च भल्लैश्च तमेकमभिदुद्रुवुः ।\nसिंहनादस्ततो घोरः पाण्डवानामजायत ॥","meaning":{"en":"with calf-tooth darts and broad arrows. Then a terrible lion's roar rose from the Pandavas."}},{"n":69,"text":"तथैव तव पुत्राश्च राजन्भीष्मजयैषिणः ।\nतमेकमभ्यवर्तन्त सिंहनादांश्च नेदिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise your sons, king, wishing for Bhishma's victory, advanced against that one man and roared like lions."}},{"n":70,"text":"तत्रासीत्तुमुलं युद्धं तावकानां परैः सह ।\nदशमेऽहनि राजेन्द्र भीष्मार्जुनसमागमे ॥","meaning":{"en":"A tumultuous battle took place there between your men and the enemy on the tenth day, king of kings, when Bhishma and Arjuna met."}},{"n":71,"text":"आसीद्गाङ्ग इवावर्तो मुहूर्तमुदधेरिव ।\nसैन्यानां युध्यमानानां निघ्नतामितरेतरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For a moment the armies, fighting and killing each other, seemed like a whirlpool where the Ganga meets the sea."}},{"n":72,"text":"अगम्यरूपा पृथिवी शोणिताक्ता तदाभवत् ।\nसमं च विषमं चैव न प्राज्ञायत किंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"The earth, stained with blood, became impassable, and nothing could be told as level or uneven."}},{"n":73,"text":"योधानामयुतं हत्वा तस्मिन्स दशमेऽहनि ।\nअतिष्ठदाहवे भीष्मो भिद्यमानेषु मर्मसु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having killed ten thousand warriors on that tenth day, Bhishma stood in the battle though his vital parts were being pierced."}},{"n":74,"text":"ततः सेनामुखे तस्मिन्स्थितः पार्थो धनंजयः ।\nमध्येन कुरुसैन्यानां द्रावयामास वाहिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Arjuna, standing at the front of the army, drove the force of the Kurus before him, right through their middle."}},{"n":75,"text":"वयं श्वेतहयाद्भीताः कुन्तीपुत्राद्धनंजयात् ।\nपीड्यमानाः शितैः शस्त्रैः प्रद्रवाम महारणात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"We, frightened of the white-horsed Dhananjaya, son of Kunti, and harassed by his sharp weapons, fled from the great battle."}},{"n":76,"text":"सौवीराः कितवाः प्राच्याः प्रतीच्योदीच्यमालवाः ।\nअभीषाहाः शूरसेनाः शिबयोऽथ वसातयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Sauviras, Kitavas, easterners, westerners, northerners, Malavas, Abhishahas, Shurasenas, Shibis and Vasatis,"}},{"n":77,"text":"शाल्वाश्रयास्त्रिगर्ताश्च अम्बष्ठाः केकयैः सह ।\nद्वादशैते जनपदाः शरार्ता व्रणपीडिताः ।\nसंग्रामे न जहुर्भीष्मं युध्यमानं किरीटिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"the Shalva allies, Trigartas and Ambashthas with the Kekayas: these twelve peoples, hurt by arrows and in pain from wounds, still did not abandon Bhishma as he fought Arjuna."}},{"n":78,"text":"ततस्तमेकं बहवः परिवार्य समन्ततः ।\nपरिकाल्य कुरून्सर्वाञ्शरवर्षैरवाकिरन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then many surrounded him, one man, and, driving all the Kurus back, covered him with showers of arrows."}},{"n":79,"text":"निपातयत गृह्णीत विध्यताथ च कर्षत ।\nइत्यासीत्तुमुलः शब्दो राजन्भीष्मरथं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Throw him down! Seize him! Pierce him! Drag him!\" Such was the tumult of cries, king, toward Bhishma's chariot."}},{"n":80,"text":"अभिहत्य शरौघैस्तं शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ।\nन तस्यासीदनिर्भिन्नं गात्रेष्वङ्गुलमात्रकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck by hundreds and thousands of floods of arrows, there was not a finger's breadth of his body left unpierced."}},{"n":81,"text":"एवं विभो तव पिता शरैर्विशकलीकृतः ।\nशिताग्रैः फल्गुनेनाजौ प्राक्शिराः प्रापतद्रथात् ।\nकिंचिच्छेषे दिनकरे पुत्राणां तव पश्यताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So your father, lord, torn to pieces by Phalguna's sharp arrows in the battle, fell headfirst from his chariot while a little of the day remained, as your sons watched."}},{"n":82,"text":"हा हेति दिवि देवानां पार्थिवानां च सर्वशः ।\nपतमाने रथाद्भीष्मे बभूव सुमहान्स्वनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A great cry of \"Alas!\" went up from the gods in the sky and from the kings everywhere as Bhishma fell from the chariot."}},{"n":83,"text":"तं पतन्तमभिप्रेक्ष्य महात्मानं पितामहम् ।\nसह भीष्मेण सर्वेषां प्रापतन्हृदयानि नः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the great-souled grandsire falling, all our hearts fell with Bhishma."}},{"n":84,"text":"स पपात महाबाहुर्वसुधामनुनादयन् ।\nइन्द्रध्वज इवोत्सृष्टः केतुः सर्वधनुष्मताम् ।\nधरणीं नास्पृशच्चापि शरसंघैः समाचितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty-armed hero fell, making the earth resound, like Indra's banner thrown down, the standard of all archers; and he did not touch the ground, being held up by the mass of arrows."}},{"n":85,"text":"शरतल्पे महेष्वासं शयानं पुरुषर्षभम् ।\nरथात्प्रपतितं चैनं दिव्यो भावः समाविशत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the great archer, the bull among men, lay on his bed of arrows, fallen from his chariot, a divine state came over him."}},{"n":86,"text":"अभ्यवर्षत पर्जन्यः प्राकम्पत च मेदिनी ।\nपतन्स ददृशे चापि खर्वितं च दिवाकरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rain fell, the earth shook, and as he fell, the sun was seen to dim."}},{"n":87,"text":"संज्ञां चैवालभद्वीरः कालं संचिन्त्य भारत ।\nअन्तरिक्षे च शुश्राव दिव्यां वाचं समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The hero recovered his senses, thinking of the time, Bharata, and he heard a divine voice from the sky all around."}},{"n":88,"text":"कथं महात्मा गाङ्गेयः सर्वशस्त्रभृतां वरः ।\nकालं कर्ता नरव्याघ्रः संप्राप्ते दक्षिणायने ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"How can the great-souled son of Ganga, the best of all who bear weapons, tiger among men, choose his time to die when the sun has just entered the southern course?\""}},{"n":89,"text":"स्थितोऽस्मीति च गाङ्गेयस्तच्छ्रुत्वा वाक्यमब्रवीत् ।\nधारयामास च प्राणान्पतितोऽपि हि भूतले ।\nउत्तरायणमन्विच्छन्भीष्मः कुरुपितामहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that, the son of Ganga said, \"I am still here,\" and though fallen on the ground, Bhishma, grandsire of the Kurus, held on to his life, wishing for the sun's northern course."}},{"n":90,"text":"तस्य तन्मतमाज्ञाय गङ्गा हिमवतः सुता ।\nमहर्षीन्हंसरूपेण प्रेषयामास तत्र वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"Understanding his wish, Ganga, the daughter of the Himalaya, sent the great sages there in the form of swans."}},{"n":91,"text":"ततः संपातिनो हंसास्त्वरिता मानसौकसः ।\nआजग्मुः सहिता द्रष्टुं भीष्मं कुरुपितामहम् ।\nयत्र शेते नरश्रेष्ठः शरतल्पे पितामहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then swans that fly far, dwellers of Lake Manasa, came quickly together to see Bhishma, the grandsire of the Kurus, where the grandsire, best of men, lay on his bed of arrows."}},{"n":92,"text":"ते तु भीष्मं समासाद्य मुनयो हंसरूपिणः ।\nअपश्यञ्शरतल्पस्थं भीष्मं कुरुपितामहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching Bhishma, those sages in swan forms saw Bhishma, grandsire of the Kurus, lying on the bed of arrows."}},{"n":93,"text":"ते तं दृष्ट्वा महात्मानं कृत्वा चापि प्रदक्षिणम् ।\nगाङ्गेयं भरतश्रेष्ठं दक्षिणेन च भास्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the great-souled one, they circled the son of Ganga, best of the Bharatas, keeping their right sides to him, and to the sun to the south."}},{"n":94,"text":"इतरेतरमामन्त्र्य प्राहुस्तत्र मनीषिणः ।\nभीष्म एव महात्मा सन्संस्थाता दक्षिणायने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking leave of one another, those wise ones said, \"Though Bhishma is high-souled, he has chosen to die while the sun is in the south.\""}},{"n":95,"text":"इत्युक्त्वा प्रस्थितान्हंसान्दक्षिणामभितो दिशम् ।\nसंप्रेक्ष्य वै महाबुद्धिश्चिन्तयित्वा च भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"After saying this, the swans set out toward the south. Seeing them, great-minded Bhishma reflected, Bharata,"}},{"n":96,"text":"तानब्रवीच्छांतनवो नाहं गन्ता कथंचन ।\nदक्षिणावृत्त आदित्ये एतन्मे मनसि स्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"and the son of Shantanu said to them, \"I will by no means go while the sun is in the south; this is fixed in my mind."}},{"n":97,"text":"गमिष्यामि स्वकं स्थानमासीद्यन्मे पुरातनम् ।\nउदगावृत्त आदित्ये हंसाः सत्यं ब्रवीमि वः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I shall go to my own place that was mine of old when the sun turns north, swans; this I tell you truly."}},{"n":98,"text":"धारयिष्याम्यहं प्राणानुत्तरायणकाङ्क्षया ।\nऐश्वर्यभूतः प्राणानामुत्सर्गे नियतो ह्यहम् ।\nतस्मात्प्राणान्धारयिष्ये मुमूर्षुरुदगायने ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will hold on to life, wishing for the northern course. Since I have power over the departure of my life, I will keep my life, wishing to die in the sun's northern path."}},{"n":99,"text":"यश्च दत्तो वरो मह्यं पित्रा तेन महात्मना ।\nछन्दतो मृत्युरित्येवं तस्य चास्तु वरस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"And the boon my great-souled father gave me, that death should come at my will, let that boon be mine now."}},{"n":100,"text":"धारयिष्ये ततः प्राणानुत्सर्गे नियते सति ।\nइत्युक्त्वा तांस्तदा हंसानशेत शरतल्पगः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will hold on to my life until the time comes for departing.\" Having said this to the swans, he lay on his bed of arrows."}},{"n":101,"text":"एवं कुरूणां पतिते शृङ्गे भीष्मे महौजसि ।\nपाण्डवाः सृञ्जयाश्चैव सिंहनादं प्रचक्रिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, when Bhishma of great vigor, the horn of the Kurus, had fallen, the Pandavas and Srinjayas roared like lions."}},{"n":102,"text":"तस्मिन्हते महासत्त्वे भरतानाममध्यमे ।\nन किंचित्प्रत्यपद्यन्त पुत्रास्ते भरतर्षभ ।\nसंमोहश्चैव तुमुलः कुरूणामभवत्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"When that mighty man, the middle one of the Bharatas, had fallen, your sons, best of the Bharatas, could think of nothing to do, and a great bewilderment came over the Kurus."}},{"n":103,"text":"नृपा दुर्योधनमुखा निःश्वस्य रुरुदुस्ततः ।\nविषादाच्च चिरं कालमतिष्ठन्विगतेन्द्रियाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The kings led by Duryodhana sighed and wept, and for a long time they stood overcome by grief, their senses gone."}},{"n":104,"text":"दध्युश्चैव महाराज न युद्धे दधिरे मनः ।\nऊरुग्राहगृहीताश्च नाभ्यधावन्त पाण्डवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They brooded, great king, and had no mind for battle. Paralyzed as if their thighs were gripped, they did not rush at the Pandavas."}},{"n":105,"text":"अवध्ये शंतनोः पुत्रे हते भीष्मे महौजसि ।\nअभावः सुमहान्राजन्कुरूनागादतन्द्रितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Bhishma, son of Shantanu, the great and unkillable, was killed, a great void came over the Kurus, who had been tireless."}},{"n":106,"text":"हतप्रवीराश्च वयं निकृत्ताश्च शितैः शरैः ।\nकर्तव्यं नाभिजानीमो निर्जिताः सव्यसाचिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Our heroes are slain, we are cut by sharp arrows and beaten by Savyasachi; we do not know what to do.\""}},{"n":107,"text":"पाण्डवास्तु जयं लब्ध्वा परत्र च परां गतिम् ।\nसर्वे दध्मुर्महाशङ्खाञ्शूराः परिघबाहवः ।\nसोमकाश्च सपञ्चालाः प्राहृष्यन्त जनेश्वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"But the Pandavas, having won victory and a high state beyond, all blew their great conches, those heroes with arms like iron bars; and the Somakas and Panchalas rejoiced, lord of men."}},{"n":108,"text":"ततस्तूर्यसहस्रेषु नदत्सु सुमहाबलः ।\nआस्फोटयामास भृशं भीमसेनो ननर्त च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, as thousands of trumpets sounded, mighty Bhimasena slapped his arms loudly and danced."}},{"n":109,"text":"सेनयोरुभयोश्चापि गाङ्गेये विनिपातिते ।\nसंन्यस्य वीराः शस्त्राणि प्राध्यायन्त समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the son of Ganga was struck down, the heroes in both armies laid down their weapons and brooded all around."}},{"n":110,"text":"प्राक्रोशन्प्रापतंश्चान्ये जग्मुर्मोहं तथापरे ।\nक्षत्रं चान्येऽभ्यनिन्दन्त भीष्मं चैकेऽभ्यपूजयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some cried out, others fell, others fainted; some blamed the warrior's code, and some honored Bhishma."}},{"n":111,"text":"ऋषयः पितरश्चैव प्रशशंसुर्महाव्रतम् ।\nभरतानां च ये पूर्वे ते चैनं प्रशशंसिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sages and the ancestors praised that man of great vows, and the earlier Bharatas also praised him."}},{"n":112,"text":"महोपनिषदं चैव योगमास्थाय वीर्यवान् ।\nजपञ्शांतनवो धीमान्कालाकाङ्क्षी स्थितोऽभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Practicing yoga, with the great Upanishad in mind, the wise and powerful son of Shantanu lay there reciting it, waiting for the time."}}]}]}